## Protocol & State Machine Architecture

### 1. Packet Types (`PacketType.kt`)

- `TRACK_REQUEST`: Sent by Requester $\to$ Target.
  ```json
  {
    "requestId": "uuid-...",
    "requesterName": "Alice",
    "timeoutSeconds": 30,
    "timestamp": 1727048400000
  }
  ```
- `TRACK_RESPONSE`: Sent by Target $\to$ Requester.
  ```json
  {
    "requestId": "uuid-...",
    "status": "ACCEPTED" | "DENIED" | "AUTO_ACCEPTED",
    "targetLat": 12.9716,
    "targetLng": 77.5946,
    "accuracy": 12.5
  }
  ```
- `TRACK_BEACON`: High-frequency periodic chirp (1.5s interval) broadcast by Target once tracking is active.
  ```json
  {
    "requestId": "uuid-...",
    "lat": 12.9716,
    "lng": 77.5946,
    "batteryLevel": 85,
    "seq": 42
  }
  ```
- `TRACK_STOP`: Sent by either Requester or Target to terminate the tracking session.

---

### 2. State Machine

```
[Requester]                                               [Target]
     │                                                        │
     ├──────────── TRACK_REQUEST (30s Timer) ────────────────>│
     │                                                        │ ──> Starts 30s Countdown Alert
     │                                                        │     [DENY] / [ACCEPT]
     │                                                        │
     │<─────────── TRACK_RESPONSE(DENIED) ────────────────────┤ (If Target taps Deny)
 [Aborted]                                                    │
     │                                                        │
     │<─────────── TRACK_RESPONSE(ACCEPTED / AUTO) ───────────┤ (Tapped Accept OR 30s Expires)
     │                                                        │
[TRACKING ACTIVE]                                    [BEACONING ACTIVE]
  - Samples RSSI on every beacon                       - Emits TRACK_BEACON every 1.5s
  - Updates Proximity Bar & Hot/Cold Geiger            - Includes GPS if available
     │                                                        │
     ├────────────────── TRACK_STOP ─────────────────────────>│
[Session Ended]                                      [Session Ended]
```

