### Component 2: Trilateration Math Engine

#### [NEW] [`MeshTrilaterationSolver.kt`](file:///c:/Users/ACER/AndroidStudioProjects/gridzero/app/src/main/java/com/example/zerogrid/mesh/tracking/MeshTrilaterationSolver.kt)

- Computes distances from RSSI using the Log-Distance Path Loss model:
  $$d = 10^{\frac{A - \text{RSSI}}{10 \cdot n}}$$
  (where $A \approx -59\text{ dBm}$ at 1 meter, $n \approx 2.4$).
- Implements **2D Weighted Least Squares (WLS) Multilateration**:
  - Accepts a list of anchors: $[(lat_1, lng_1, r_1, \text{weight}_1), (lat_2, lng_2, r_2, \text{weight}_2), \dots]$.
  - Converts WGS84 GPS coordinates to local Cartesian coordinates (tangent plane in meters).
  - Uses linear matrix reduction:
    $$2(x_i - x_1)x + 2(y_i - y_1)y = (r_1^2 - r_i^2) + (x_i^2 + y_i^2) - (x_1^2 + y_1^2)$$
  - Solves for $(x, y)$ using pseudo-inverse with weights proportional to signal strength ($\text{weight}_i = 1 / d_i$).
  - Converts $(x, y)$ back to $(lat, lng)$ with an estimated accuracy circle in meters.

